// Application-level settings for the iOS Runner target — the edition seam,
// mirroring macos/Runner/Configs/AppInfo.xcconfig (docs/releases.md §2.6, §8).
// Included by ios/Flutter/{Debug,Release}.xcconfig, so it feeds both the
// pbxproj (which builds PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER / the app-icon set name from
// $(HALO_EDITION)) and Info.plist (CFBundleDisplayName = $(HALO_DISPLAY_NAME)).

// --- Edition selection ---------------------------------------------------------
// Picks which app this build is. Defaults to `dev` — the plain, build-it-
// yourself edition — so a plain build (and every public checkout) produces Dev.
// CI selects an official edition by writing `HALO_EDITION = next` (or `prod`)
// into Local.xcconfig at build time; xcconfig resolves values lazily, so that
// override (included last) still drives the names/id below.
HALO_EDITION = dev

// Per-edition home-screen label. It sits under the app icon (which already
// carries the "Ham2K" mark), so per the branding rule it drops the "Ham2K"
// prefix and names the platform: "Portable Logger" (+ edition) on iOS/Android.
HALO_PRODUCT_NAME_dev = Portable Logger (Dev)
HALO_PRODUCT_NAME_next = Portable Logger Next
HALO_PRODUCT_NAME_prod = Portable Logger

// Selected by nested substitution and consumed by Info.plist's
// CFBundleDisplayName / CFBundleName.
HALO_DISPLAY_NAME = $(HALO_PRODUCT_NAME_$(HALO_EDITION))
